  "description": "PEQFEX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C70 H54 Br6 Cl1 N6 O16 Yb3,0.5(C2 H3 N1),1.5(C1 H4 O1),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 7 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 4 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 4 O neighbors; Yb5 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb6 (Yb) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.693-3.896 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 107.20-114.59°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Yb3L3(OAc)2Cl](H2O)3(CH3OH)1.5(CH3CN)0.5 (H2L = N,N'-bis(5-bromo-3-methoxysalicylidene)phenylene-1,2-diamine). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
